WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.460
What do you know about the Georgetown sale of the 272 slaves?

2
00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:06.720
Outside of the family tree.

3
00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:09.120
How does it make you feel?

4
00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:16.240
To be honest, it’s kind of . . . I hate to say . . . You don’t want to say hate.

5
00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:21.220
But it just give you a bad feeling to know this is what happened.

6
00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:23.300
But then it’s not just the Georgetown.

7
00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:24.860
I mean, this was worldwide.

8
00:00:24.860 --> 00:00:26.740
It was everywhere.

9
00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:30.140
But the slaves that they were selling them—you hate knowing that.

10
00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:33.740
Okay, this is a Christian institute, that they would do something like that.

11
00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:37.680
But then I try not to be angry, because that’s life.

12
00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:42.160
But sometime when you think about it, you just get . . . I’m fixing to say pissed,

13
00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:45.940
but [laughs] you get . . . you really kind of just get angry.

14
00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:50.920
But I mean, the older you get, you just come to: Okay, that’s life.

15
00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:51.700
This is what happens.

16
00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:52.560
Nothing you can do about it.

17
00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:54.800
Now that’s really . . . That’s irritating, because you cannot go back.

18
00:00:54.800 --> 00:01:01.660
I can’t go back and say, “Okay, I know where my people . . . my great-great-grandfathers and stuff come from,” because I really don’t.

19
00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:04.720
You just have to kind of shake it off and go on.
